   ],
   "textLength": 1122,
   "text": "When you’re small, friction is manageable. A two-person engineering team can keep track of their work in their heads, coordinate through chat, and still ship quickly. But as organizations scale, these small points of friction don’t just add up, they multiply.\n“Ship yesterday” characterizes the engineering organization at OpenAI. Engineers might work on eight different products in a single year as ",
